 "note": "The south end of the shops on the east side, one OSM footprint of three buildings (Main Street Historic Walk sites 34-36): The Tuckshop (the old Nixon electrical and bike shop, a small gabled building with its name painted on the roof), the dark ANZ and Morries building (on the 1935 Owen-Tucker house site: a flat-roofed block behind a tall charcoal street front with a gabled parapet over the north end and a blue band along the shopfront), and Arc of Iris (the 1928-29 McLeod and Auger grocery site) under an olive-green hip roof with a lean-to verandah. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and 2019 street photos. Names in plain lettering, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from Bussell Hwy (north to south), y back (east) from the ANZ front.",
